    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an `AUDIT` log line on successful owner creation containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\nTo keep structural impact minimal, I avoided touching the complex `addOwner` controller method (high CC, large surrounding class WMC) and the large `Owner` class's methods. Instead:\n\n1. **New tiny cohesive class** \u2014 `model/OwnerAuditListener.java`: a JPA entity listener with a single `@PostPersist` method (CC=1, no surrounding methods) that logs to the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`. It fires exactly when a new owner is inserted, with the id, customerCode, and registrationDate all populated at that point.\n\n2. **One class-level annotation** on `Owner` \u2014 `@EntityListeners(OwnerAuditListener.class)`. This is not a function-body change, and `@EntityListeners` was already covered by the existing `jakarta.persistence.*` import, so no import churn either.\n\nThis adds the behaviour as a small, self-contained unit with essentially zero cyclomatic complexity and no growth to any existing method or class \u2014 the biggest lever (WMC_other) is untouched because no complex method was edited.\n\nResult: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-04`, and `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
